PRETABLE -- #529 crimewidthkill, KILL TABLE 12: REPAIR 14 (the class closure Fable ruled, 204 rows predicted).
Written BEFORE the table: this file's mtime precedes the driver, every build log and every probe log.
MANDATORY under the 2026-08-28 flagship ruling for any round shipping or EXTENDING a kill-table-backed
detector, and recorded as OUTPUT rather than asserted.

*** AND THIS BLOCK HAS ALREADY EARNED ITS KEEP ONCE, BEFORE THE TABLE RUNS. ***  Drafting the predicted red
rows below showed that NOTHING in the repair moved under either K_ctl*w_reset_post mutant: every accepted
CONTROL write in the probe carried 0x01, 0x0001 or 0x0201 and none carried HARD_RESET 0x800.  The
generating-set cells were still open in a diff written specifically to close them.  Six rows and three
sessions were added as a result.  *Had the table run first it would have reported two escapes I had
already been told about, and the ask-again would have been spent naming a hole I put there.*

================================================================================================================
INSTRUMENT
================================================================================================================
  regress/crime_width_probe.py after repair 14, frozen by the driver.  188 rows before, SIXTEEN added:

      c t4w gap / c t4r gap / c t gap once      entries 32 and 33, latch CLEAR, gapped clock-advance
      acc istat lw / p acc istat lw             entry 21, BOTH latch states, seeded above bit 31
      top8 clear                                entry 46, latch CLEAR
      acc ctl4r / acc ctl0c + the POST twins    CONTROL 4R as a PAIR, both latch states
      rst alive / rst alive once                the halt oracle's liveness control
      rst 4w / rst 4w once / rst 8w / rst 8w once   the HARD_RESET generating-set cells

  **THE BASE LEG MUST REPORT 204/204.**  That number is DERIVED (188 + 16, counted from the row() sites with
  loop templates expanded) and is PREDICTED here, not asserted: the base run confirms it or the count is
  wrong.  Entry 14 adds NO row -- it changes `p acc ctl msg' from 3 to 4 -- so 204 is also the check that
  nothing was added twice.

  *** ONE THING THE STATIC COUNT CANNOT SETTLE, and it is owed to the base leg: six row-name LITERALS in this
  probe are FORMAT TEMPLATES expanded in loops.  Whether every expansion is DISTINCT at runtime is only
  checkable by running.  A duplicate name does not fail loudly -- it makes a gate's grep ambiguous, which is
  the padded-column trap's cousin. ***

================================================================================================================
WHAT CHANGED, and the disposition of every cell the panel named
================================================================================================================
  ROWED NOW: entries 14, 21 (both latch states), 32, 33, 46, the CONTROL 4R pair, and the two HARD_RESET
  generating-set cells.
  EQUIVALENT with the derivation in the contract, no row owed: entries 1, 3 (the prelude re-forces REV and
  it is read nowhere else); 4, 8 (the 4-byte read takes the HIGH lane and answers 0, and so does a decline).
  HOST-DIAGNOSTIC: entry 40.
  NO EXISTING SESSION'S COMMAND LIST WAS SHORTENED OR REORDERED.  Three sessions were ADDED (the halt
  sessions, which must end at their write) and four existing sessions gained accesses.

  TARGETING: this is NOT adds-only -- four existing sessions changed -- so the targeting rule does NOT
  exempt the earlier tables' kills.  **Every leg below is re-run against the 204-row instrument.**

================================================================================================================
PRE-TABLE CHECK 1 -- SIBLING PARITY
================================================================================================================
  The twin sessions (pre-latch and POST) are the sibling pair here, and repair 14 kept them SYMMETRIC: every
  access added to one was added to the other (entry 21's lw, the CONTROL 4R pair).  That symmetry is the
  point -- it is what makes a latch-keyed decline move exactly one row of each pair.
  ASYMMETRIES, both deliberate and both recorded:
    * entry 46 gained a CLEAR row only.  Its POST half was ALREADY rowed (`top8 st+ld'), which is why the
      cell read as blind: it was observed in one state only.
    * the HARD_RESET cells are POST-only.  There is no CLEAR twin because the latch must be SET for the
      cell to exist -- a session that has not refused is not in that state at all.

================================================================================================================
PRE-TABLE CHECK 2 -- CLAIM -> ROW (semantic: does this added sentence assert something a row could see?)
================================================================================================================
  "the 4-byte read takes the HIGH lane and answers 0"              -> `acc ctl4r' / `p acc ctl4r' (want 0)
                                                                      AND `acc ctl0c' / `p acc ctl0c' (0x100),
                                                                      which is what makes the first pair
                                                                      non-vacuous.
  "seeding below bit 31 would make the row answer 0"               -> `acc istat lw' wants BIT >> 32.
  "an accepted 0x800 stops every CPU"                              -> `rst 4w' / `rst 8w' want the SENTINEL,
                                                                      with `rst alive' as the liveness half.
  "the latch stays CLEAR in these sessions"                        -> `c t gap once' wants [0, 0].
  "entry 14's sd twin prints too"                                  -> `p acc ctl msg' 3 -> 4.
  "REV is read nowhere else in the file"                           -> EXPLICIT NO-ROW SENTENCE in the
                                                                      contract, with its grep.

