================================================================================================================
PRE-TABLE CHECK 4 -- CHANNEL.  Per new row: the mutant it kills, and the observable that differs
================================================================================================================
  acc/p acc istat lw   G_clr_ist4r (and its latch-SET sibling).  Observable: INTSTAT's HIGH 32 bits,
                       0x1010101 seeded vs 0 declined.  *** VACUOUS IF SEEDED BELOW BIT 31 -- 0 == 0. ***
  c t4w/c t4r gap      G_glm_tim4clear.  Observable: the clock-advance magnitude across the debugger's own
                       pause; ~13,000x on the shipped POST twin.
  c t gap once         not a kill row -- the CONTROL that these two sessions really are latch-CLEAR.
  top8 clear           M2_ld278clr.  Observable: the seeded 8-byte value at +0x278 before any refusal.
  acc/p acc ctl0c      G_lane_ctl.  Observable: the LOW lane, 0x100.  Its `ctl4r' partner wants 0 and is
                       VACUOUS ALONE; the pair is the row.
  rst 4w / rst 8w      K_ctl4w_reset_post / K_ctl8w_reset_post.  Observable: THE HALT -- v1 keeps the
                       SENTINEL because the round trip after the write never runs.
                       *** `absent' would mean the HOST died, which is the defect #529 REMOVED; a row
                       wanting `absent' would go GREEN when the fix was reverted. ***
  rst alive            the liveness half: with no 0x800 the round trip completes and v1 holds LIVE_VAL.
  p acc ctl msg (4)    a decline of the 8-byte CONTROL write.  Observable: the COUNT, because the `sd' and
                       `sw' forms print TEXT-IDENTICAL messages -- checked at dev_sgi_ip32.c:361-379.

