    G_glm_tim4clear   reds c t4w gap, c t4r gap                          202/204
    G_clr_ist4r       reds acc istat lw                                  203/204
    G_lane_ctl        reds acc ctl4r, acc ctl0c, p acc ctl4r, p acc ctl0c 200/204
    K_ctl4w_reset_post  reds rst 4w                                      203/204
    K_ctl8w_reset_post  reds rst 8w                                      203/204
    M2_ld278clr       reds top8 clear                                    203/204
    W_ctl8w           reds p acc ctl msg AND rst 8w                     202/204
                      *** ENTRY 14 HAD NO MUTANT UNTIL NOW, WHICH MEANS ITS ROW HAD NEVER BEEN SHOWN TO
                      FAIL.  mutants_r14.py supplies the width-axis (d) form: decline the EIGHT-byte
                      CONTROL WRITE, post-latch only.  TWO rows fall, and tracing them is what showed the
                      second: the POST session issues sd 0x01 AND sd 0x0201, so the count goes 4 -> 2; and
                      rst_session(sd) writes 0x800 at CONTROL post-latch, so a decline means the CPUs do
                      NOT stop and the round trip after it RUNS.  Deliberately NOT red: the 4-byte halt
                      (rst 4w) still works -- which is what makes this a WIDTH mutant rather than a
                      CONTROL-write one -- and the CLEAR twin acc ctl sd is untouched by the latch term.

  MUST NOT MOVE (the controls that make the kills mean something):
    base              204/204, CONTROL=OK
    G_clr_imk4r       still KILLED on `gate line' -- *** grok's constraint: it is the CLEAR-half positive
                      control that is not TIME, and repair 14 must not disturb what gate line observes ***
    G_clr_ctl4r       still 204/204 -- the equivalent cell, now with the ctl0c pair able to see a lane edit

  *** PREDICTED TO STILL ESCAPE, DISCLOSED IN ADVANCE RATHER THAN DISCOVERED: ***
    M3_timelatch      204/204   the decline-suppression face at TIME
    M5_revlatch       204/204   the same at REV
  Their carriers are DELIBERATELY NOT IN THIS DIFF.  Fable's ruling requires them to observe the SUPPRESSED
  ARM, and the measuring seat needed four mutants to find that face at all -- a carrier written blind against
  a channel nobody has measured is how a vacuous row ships.  **The contract in the probe header says so in as
  many words, so these two are `outside the contract, as stated' rather than breaches.**  M4_timeplain
  (184/188) and M6_istlatch (185/188) remain the controls showing the detector CAN see that shape.

  THE CLOSING CONDITION, stated before the run so it cannot be fitted afterwards: this pass closes the
  ACCEPT-side class only.  It closes when all six mutants above are killed on their named rows, the three
  controls do not move, and the base reports 204/204.  **The decline-suppression face stays OPEN and named.**

A red row outside its prediction is RE-RUN ALONE before it is believed.
